<Base title="Advik Sharma">
  <h1>I write software that runs close to the hardware, and I test it before it flies.</h1>
  <p>I'm a computer engineering student at the University of Washington. Most of what I build is C++ for microcontrollers, with some SystemVerilog and a fair amount of Python for data work.</p>
  <p>I'm looking for a 2027 software internship, embedded and systems roles especially. The easiest way to reach me is <a href="mailto:adviks.work@outlook.com">email</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="work">Work</h2>
  <ul class="work">
    <li><span class="when">Nov 2026</span><span><a class="t" href="/projects/lunar-listings/">Lunar Listings</a><br><span class="d">A Zillow-style site for the Moon where every price comes from NASA data. NASA Space Apps, team of three.</span></span></li>
    <li><span class="when">Summer 2026 to now</span><span><a class="t" href="/projects/quadrotor/">Quadrotor flight software</a><br><span class="d">Estimation, control and a flight state machine in bare-metal C++, with no flight-control libraries.</span></span></li>
    <li><span class="when">2025 to now</span><span><a class="t" href="/projects/fixed-wing/">Fixed-wing UAV</a><br><span class="d">Telemetry lead, now project lead, at UW's Autonomous Flight Club.</span></span></li>
    <li><span class="when">Spring 2026</span><span><a class="t" href="/projects/fpga-snake/">Snake on an FPGA</a><br><span class="d">The game in SystemVerilog, with an NES controller and an LED matrix.</span></span></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Tools</h2>
  <p class="small">C++, C, Python, MATLAB, SystemVerilog, Java. PlatformIO, FreeRTOS, Git, Linux, Quartus, ModelSim.</p>
